=== prefab_item_hidens_powercell
metadata:``` yaml
type: item/resource/energy
key: hidens_powercell
display_text: HiDens Power Cell
art: container_2a
mode: resource
targets: ship, cockpit
price: 150
desc: Instantly restores 500 ship energy when used.
pickup_trigger: __player__
```
    blob = to_blob(UPGRADE_AGENT_ID)
    if blob is not None:
        blob.set("energy", blob.get("energy", 0) + 500, 0)
    ->END

=== prefab_item_vigoranium_nodule
metadata:``` yaml
type: item/upgrade/engineering
key: vigoranium_nodule
display_text: Vigoranium Nodule
art: container_4a
mode: consumable
targets: ship, cockpit
consoles: engineering
duration: 5
tier: 2
price: 250
desc: Restores damage-control team strength.
```
    # Applied inline, like every other item effect. item_activate.mast is already
    # //shared/signal (server-only, once) and runs this label inside that route, so a
    # second signal would only add a hop where a //signal handler could later race one
    # damcon SPAWN per connected console. The signal this used to emit had no handler
    # anywhere, which made the nodule a silent no-op.
    #
    # Deliberately NOT reproducing LM13's "refuse at full strength, do not consume":
    # item_activate decrements the count before this label runs, so by now the nodule is
    # already spent. Wasting one at full strength matches every other consumable.
    # Guard the holder: comms_broadcast to a non-live ship raises "invalid space object"
    # (SendMessageToPlayerShip) in the engine, and a py-side role can outlive the ship by a
    # tick - see items/item_collect.mast for the same guard.
    ->END if sim.get_space_object(UPGRADE_AGENT_ID) is None
    grid_restore_damcons(UPGRADE_AGENT_ID)
    comms_broadcast(UPGRADE_AGENT_ID, "Vigoranium Nodule spent - damage control teams restored", "#ff0", category="ship")
    ->END

